      "lineNbr": 1451,
      "author": {
        "id": 1863140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-30T00:59:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are right. My understanding is that the license lines were added recently in a consistent way. When the license lines were added to the Make modules on the same file, the same license lines had been added. Please correct me if I am wrong, bbadour@. So in this version, I just convert the license part from the first module if there are more than one modules on the same file.\n\nI was planning to convert the licenses for all the modules, or each module will have a license module. Then compare these license modules. If all of them are the same, then just move all of them except the first one; if observe diff, report an error. (the comparison can be done without generating the license modules as well, by using the converted content from the androidmk process.).\n\nBut the question is, if different licenses are observed for different module in the same Android.mk file, how do we handle it?\n\nBack to my understanding on the top, I think there should be no such case (different licenses are observed for different module in the same Android.mk file).",
      "parentUuid": "37027b0c_cc854d40",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1451,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 1451,
        "endChar": 29
